VolytraFly for RusherHack
==========================

The flight logic, settings, highway navigation, player avoidance, and HUD
behaviour in this plugin are a port of VolytraFly-Addon by Volizray:

    https://github.com/Volizray/VolytraFly-Addon

That project is dedicated to the public domain under the CC0 1.0 Universal
public domain dedication. A copy of that dedication is in LICENSE.

VolytraFly-Addon was built from the Meteor Addon Template
(https://github.com/MeteorDevelopment/meteor-addon-template) and runs as a
Meteor Client addon. This repository reimplements it against the RusherHack
plugin API. The Gradle layout follows RusherDevelopment/example-plugin
(https://github.com/RusherDevelopment/example-plugin).

The original addon icon is included at
src/main/resources/assets/volytrafly/icon.png.

VolytraFly-Addon 0.1.1, the revision this port is based on, notes:

- Speed no longer resets to min speed value after rubberbanding, but back
  along the acceleration curve (so a rubberband at 300 bps reduces speed by <1%)
- Added a rubberband speed cap, so if server speed changes while in-game,
  VolytraFly will detect and limit your speed too for smoother flight
- Added visuals, including a speedometer, fuel gauge, light switches for
  modes, Volytra assistant, and future sight
- Added bypass mode, which flies using additive acceleration to act more like
  normal elytra flight
- Removed some unnecessary features from the options like player avoidance's
  vertical step since they never really need to be changed
- Added highway mode, which uses a hybrid of mob pathfinding and custom
  navigation to travel across highways
